Executive Project Synthesis (Deliverable Summary)
Over five distinct architectural phases, this portfolio designs, optimizes, and evaluates a resilient database platform for ApexPay:
Portfolio 1 (Data Design): Built an enterprise-grade relational schema in Boyce-Codd Normal Form (BCNF), with strict database constraints enforcing double-entry ledger safety and complete entity integrity.
Portfolio 2 (Optimization): Modeled high-volume transaction queries, analyzed baseline full-table scans, and applied targeted composite and partial indexes to drop execution latency by 99.8%.
Portfolio 3 (Concurrency): Established safe transaction boundaries and isolation settings, showing how MVCC and structured row-level locking prevent deadlocks, dirty reads, and lost updates during parallel transfers.
Portfolio 4 (NoSQL): Integrated a polyglot persistence architecture, using document stores for audit logs, in-memory caches for rate limiting, and graph databases for multi-hop fraud detection.
Portfolio 5 (Distributed Cloud): Designed a globally distributed, sharded cloud database topology that uses a CP-focused Paxos consensus model to balance high availability with zero-loss financial consistency.

